diagnosis_text:
The user on pc1 (195.11.14.2) reported approximately one-in-three packets failing to reach pc2 (200.1.1.2) on the simple_bgp topology. A thorough multi-layer diagnostic sweep found no fault mechanism anywhere on the path.

**Affected component:** None — all subsystems are healthy.

**Mechanism:** Absent. A 30-packet ICMP test from pc1 to pc2 returned 0% loss with stable RTT (0.7–1.6 ms). All six path interfaces (pc1:eth0, router1:eth1/eth0, router2:eth0/eth1, pc2:eth0) carry default `fq_codel` qdiscs with no `netem` or `tbf` shaping injected. Interface hardware counters on both transit routers show zero errors, zero drops, and zero carrier events — consistent with a lab that has only handled startup-calibration traffic.

**Localization:** No device is implicated. BGP sessions between router1 (ASN 1, 195.11.14.0/24) and router2 (ASN 2, 200.1.1.0/24) are fully established with correct prefix advertisements. Infra sweep found no ACL rules, no ARP poisoning, no addressing anomalies, and no duplicate MACs. Pressure sweep found no stress tools or load generators on any device.

**Root cause:** The ~33% packet-loss report is unconfirmed; no fault mechanism, historical trace (syslog/dmesg are empty), or flap process exists on any device in the topology.

**Fix:** No corrective action is required. If the symptom reappears, re-run this diagnostic while the loss is actively occurring to capture a non-zero counter or `tc` rule. The network is healthy as of this investigation.
=== END ===